[stderr] +# GC0001 coverage checkpoint
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Scope and conclusion
[stderr] +
[stderr] +This checkpoint audits the completed `G0001`–`G0005` design-evidence wave. Its
[stderr] +canonical design coverage and dependency chain are closed, but the QB-A
[stderr] +catalogue's card-level editorial acceptance boundary is not. The manifest must
[stderr] +therefore remain pending. `GD0002` is the one bounded successor that owns every
[stderr] +item in that boundary; a later `GQ` audit, not this checkpoint, may evaluate
[stderr] +manifest completion after `GD0002` supplies the required evidence.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Ownership, cap, canonical coverage, and closure
[stderr] +
[stderr] +| Owning batch | Declared G outputs | Cap | Canonical coverage | Dependency closure |
[stderr] +| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
[stderr] +| `GB0001` | `G0001`, `G0002` | 2 of 5 | `GAME-001`–`GAME-004`; `GPI-001`–`GPI-007` | `G0002` depends on `G0001`; closed. |
[stderr] +| `GB0002` | `G0003`, `G0004` | 2 of 5 | `GAME-005`–`GAME-008`; `GPI-008`–`GPI-011` | `G0003` depends on `G0002`; `G0004` depends on `G0003`; closed. |
[stderr] +| `GB0003` | `G0005` | 1 of 5 | `GAME-009`–`GAME-012`; `GPI-012`–`GPI-015` | `G0005` depends on `G0004`; closed. |
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Each completed G task declares the same `design_authoring_batch` as its owning
[stderr] +batch's output list. The allocated canonical sets cover every `GAME-001`
[stderr] +through `GAME-012` and `GPI-001` through `GPI-015` exactly once. No rejected
[stderr] +or decision-gated module is allocated. The detailed evidence outputs are:
[stderr] +
[stderr] +- `G0001`: question-card and QB-A catalogue bible.
[stderr] +- `G0002`: adjudication and freshness bible.
[stderr] +- `G0003`: round lifecycle bible.
[stderr] +- `G0004`: score, streak, and results bible.
[stderr] +- `G0005`: accessibility, recovery, and target-parity bible.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Evidence inspected
[stderr] +
[stderr] +- `G0001` provides card grammar, original-expression and permitted-source
[stderr] +  policy, quota tables, provenance fields, and a two-review workflow for four
[stderr] +  QB-A batches. The 48 inventory records remain explicitly `draft`, have
[stderr] +  `PROV-<ID>` placeholders, and have pending review records.
[stderr] +- `G0002` provides deterministic select, true/false, ordered, and typed
[stderr] +  adjudication; 20 fixtures; withdrawal/correction lifecycle states; and
[stderr] +  seeded anti-repeat and shortage fixtures. Publication-dependent selection is
[stderr] +  conditional while no QB-A card is eligible.
[stderr] +- `G0003` provides `TUT-01`–`TUT-05` First Whistle transitions, Mixed Fixture
[stderr] +  seeded selection/shortage fixtures, an optional-off timer, offline and
[stderr] +  interruption lifecycle, and accessibility review.
[stderr] +- `G0004` provides the capped 100-point score/streak rule; wrong, blank,
[stderr] +  timeout, and abandon recovery; idempotent results/milestones; edge fixtures;
[stderr] +  and text, non-colour, captioned/muted audio-equivalent feedback.
[stderr] +- `G0005` provides touch, pointer, keyboard, and gamepad mappings;
[stderr] +  non-audio/non-colour equivalents; recovery/offline/update states; and
[stderr] +  shared-rule, shared-content, shared-save web/PWA/Android/iOS parity
[stderr] +  evidence.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Incomplete QB-A editorial boundary
[stderr] +
[stderr] +The following is the complete remaining evidence boundary and is owned solely
[stderr] +by `GD0002`:
[stderr] +
[stderr] +1. `GPI-001` lacks completed card-level resolvable provenance and two distinct
[stderr] +   accepted current-revision reviews for `QB-A-01`–`QB-A-48`.
[stderr] +2. `GPI-002`–`GPI-005` are each a finite 12-card `draft` batch at revision 1,
[stderr] +   with placeholder provenance and two pending reviews. Placeholder records
[stderr] +   cannot enter selection.
[stderr] +3. `GAME-002` lacks accepted original-expression, factual-source/provenance,
[stderr] +   factual/rights, accessibility/copy, and independent second-review decisions
[stderr] +   for every current card revision.
[stderr] +4. `GAME-004` and `GAME-006` have deterministic policy and fixture evidence,
[stderr] +   but published QB-A candidate use remains conditional on the accepted records
[stderr] +   above.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +There are no blocked product decisions in this wave.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Successor and manifest guardrail
[stderr] +
[stderr] +`GD0002` is the exactly one bounded successor. It is limited to an editorial
[stderr] +acceptance register for the existing 48 records in the four existing 12-card
[stderr] +batches; it may not add cards, alter quiz scope, create implementation
[stderr] +runbooks, or accept the manifest. It must retain any rejected, unresolved,
[stderr] +withdrawn, conflicted, or incompletely reviewed card as ineligible with its
[stderr] +exact reason.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +`planning/game-design-manifest.json` is intentionally still `pending`: its
[stderr] +`final_audit` is `null`, `GC0001` is a pending checkpoint, and no `GQ` final
[stderr] +manifest audit has been created. Only after `GD0002` closes every item above may
[stderr] +a later `GQ` audit run the dedicated completion check, update canonical
[stderr] +bible/inventory records, and accept the manifest.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Checkpoint result
[stderr] +
[stderr] +The five completed G tasks satisfy ownership, cap, canonical-coverage, and
[stderr] +dependency-closure checks. Their design-rule evidence is preserved, while the
[stderr] +single unclosed QB-A editorial acceptance boundary is accurately deferred to
[stderr] +`GD0002`; manifest acceptance is deliberately deferred to a later `GQ` audit.
