ity/copy review, independent second\n  review, and resulting lifecycle status.\n- Update `design-evidence/question-card-and-qba-catalogue-bible.md` only as\n  needed to point to the register and replace the explicitly pending catalogue\n  state after all 48 records qualify. Preserve its existing quotas, IDs, and\n  source policy.\n\nThe successor must leave rejected, unresolved, withdrawn, conflicted, or\nincompletely reviewed cards ineligible and state the exact reason. It must not\nset `planning/game-design-manifest.json` to accepted. A later `GQ` audit is the\nonly task allowed to run the dedicated completion check, update canonical\nbible/inventory records, and accept that manifest.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- All 48 existing QB-A card revisions have independently inspectable\n  original-expression, provenance, and two-distinct-review evidence, or every\n  remaining ineligible card has its exact pending or blocked reason retained.\n- The four existing batches remain finite at 12 cards each and no unreviewed\n  record can enter selection.\n{\n  \"status\": \"pending\",\n  \"final_audit\": null,\n  \"pending_modules\": [\"quiz-content-and-editorial-integrity\", \"round-score-and-progress-rules\", \"accessible-recoverable-multitarget-experience\"],\n  \"blocked_modules\": [],\n  \"checkpoint\": {\n    \"audit\": \"GC0001\",\n    \"status\": \"pending\",\n    \"findings\": [\n      \"Ownership is closed: GB0001 owns G0001,G0002; GB0002 owns G0003,G0004; GB0003 owns G0005. Each G declares its owning batch and each batch has fewer than five G outputs.\",\n      \"Canonical coverage is assigned and evidenced by the five detailed bibles: GAME-001 through GAME-012 and GPI-001 through GPI-015 are represented; G dependencies reference earlier available G outputs.\",\n      \"The quiz-content-and-editorial-integrity module is not accepted: QB-A-01 through QB-A-48 are explicitly draft records with only pending review records. The catalogue defines required provenance loca